      "direct_output": "We are told that **Danny and Harry share $30**, and that **Danny receives $3 for every $2 that Harry receives**.\n\nLet’s define:\n\n- Let $ x $ be the amount Harry receives.\n- Then Danny receives $ \\frac{3}{2}x $, since he gets $3 for every $2 that Harry gets.\n\nThe total amount they share is $30, so:\n\n$$\nx + \\frac{3}{2}x = 30\n$$\n\nCombine the terms:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{2}x + \\frac{3}{2}x = \\frac{5}{2}x = 30\n$$\n\nSolve for $ x $:\n\n$$\nx = \\frac{30 \\times 2}{5} = \\frac{60}{5} = 12\n$$\n\n### ✅ Final Answer:\n$$\n\\boxed{12}\n$$\n\nHarry receives **$12**.",
