      "direct_prompt_key": "33dc785635c3f261d36fefda4693caf807d9a29e7e2b1eed538eb0cdb5238c10",
      "direct_output": "We are given:\n\n- A company plants **500 trees** in a year.\n- **10% of the trees die each year**.\n- **20% of the remaining trees survive the next year**.\n\nWe are to find how many trees are left **after one year**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Trees planted at the start of the year = 500\n\n### Step 2: 10% of the trees die each year.\n\nSo, **90% of the trees survive** the first year.\n\n$$\n\\text{Surviving trees} = 500 \\times (1 - 0.10) = 500 \\times 0.90 = 450\n$$\n\n### Step 3: 20% of the remaining trees survive the next year.\n\nSo, **80% of the 450 trees survive** the second year.\n\n$$\n\\text{Surviving trees after second year} = 450 \\times (1 - 0.20) = 450 \\times 0.80 = 360\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{360}\n$$\n\nSo, **360 trees are left** after one year.",
